# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill One or two sentences on what this site does and who uses it. -->

A server-rendered Django web app, served by gunicorn with static files from whitenoise and data in SQLite.

## Quickstart

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and make.

```bash
make install
make dev          # http://127.0.0.1:8000 with reload and DEBUG on
```

Create an admin login with `uv run python manage.py createsuperuser`, then open http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make dev` | Migrate, then run the development server with reload |
| `make start` | Production settings: collectstatic, migrate, then gunicorn |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Check / fix Python and template lint and formatting |
| `make typecheck` | mypy strict with the Django plugin |
| `make test` / `make coverage` | Tests, and tests with the coverage floor |
| `make makemigrations` | Write migrations after a model change |
| `make check-deploy` | Django's deployment checklist with production settings |

Run `make help` for the full list. Settings are environment variables; `.env.example` lists them.

## Layout

```
config/     settings, env parsing, logging, urls, wsgi, gunicorn
core/       request logging middleware, health view
accounts/   the custom user model
notes/      the example app: model, admin, form, views, templates
templates/  base layout and the 404 and 500 pages
static/     project CSS
tests/      page tests through Django's test client
```

